[00:09.56]Are you all right, Lydia?
[00:11.92]No, I’m not, Dad.
[00:13.98]I’m not well at all.
[00:15.70]What’s the matter with you?
[00:17.36]I’ve got a really bad stomach ache.
[00:20.50]Do you think it was something you ate?
[00:22.84]No, not just one thing.
[00:25.20]She ate loads.
[00:26.68]Don’t be mean, Liam.
[00:28.61]Your sister doesn’t feel great.
[00:30.92]He’s right, Dad.
[00:32.78]I think I was too hungry.
[00:35.06]I didn’t have any lunch at school today.
[00:38.04]I think you need to just go and lie down for a while.
[00:42.42]I’m sure you’ll feel better soon.
[00:44.69]OK, Dad.
[00:45.86]I will.
[00:46.82]I’ll just try and rest.
[00:48.44]And don’t worry about the washing-up.
[00:50.97]I’m sure your brother will do that.
[00:53.40]What?
[00:54.20]Me??!!
[01:01.28]Come in, Tim.
[01:02.84]Take a seat.
[01:04.10]Thank you, Doctor.
[01:05.22]So how can I help you today?
[01:07.76]It’s my elbow.
[01:09.18]It’s really painful.
[01:10.82]Look.
[01:11.50]Hmm, yes, it does look a bit bruised.
[01:16.72]So what happened?
[01:18.52]Well, it’s a bit of a silly story really.
[01:21.64]I got home from school yesterday and I didn’t have my key with me.
[01:25.50]I left it in my locker at school so I tried to open the door with my elbow.
[01:31.42]Oh, I see.
[01:34.04]And it didn’t open?
[01:36.80]No, it didn’t.
[01:38.62]Well, I don’t think it’s anything too serious.
[01:42.20]You need to put some ice on it, and take some painkillers if it hurts too much.
[01:47.66]So, it’s not broken?
[01:49.88]No, it isn’t.
[01:51.58]You’re able to move it so I’m not too worried.
[01:54.42]But next time you forget your key, just wait for your parents to get home.
[02:00.56]OK, Doctor.
[02:01.80]I will.
[02:08.80]Hello, John.
[02:10.52]What can I do for you?
[02:12.10]It’s my neck.
[02:13.70]OK.
[02:15.06]And what’s the problem with it?
[02:17.62]Does it hurt?
[02:18.70]Yes, it does.
[02:20.20]I can hardly move it.
[02:21.62]Oh dear.
[02:23.26]What happened?
[02:24.80]I’m not sure.
[02:26.32]I went to bed last night and when I woke up it was really hurting.
[02:33.06]Did you do any sport yesterday?
[02:36.58]No, I didn’t.
[02:38.48]But I did sleep with the window open.
[02:41.74]My grandmother thinks the cold air made it hurt but I’m not so sure.
[02:47.47]No, I don’t think there’s any connection there.
[02:51.66]OK, well, let’s have a look at it.
[02:55.56]Can you take your shirt off for me, please?
[02:58.46]Sure.
